<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Atamu Tekena</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1892</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Atamu Tekena was ariki, or king, of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/easter-island">Rapa Nui</a> (Easter Island) in the late 19th century. On 9 September 1888 he signed the agreement with the Chilean naval captain <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/policarpo-toro">Policarpo Toro</a> by which Chile annexed the island. Rapa Nui remains part of Chile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/atamu-tekena.jpg" alt="Atamu Tekena" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edward Schonsett from Henderson, Nevada, USA · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bust_of_Atamu_Tekena_(10772100486).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
